@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
    ViewData["Description"] = "What this version of Portico stores. A reservation here is a preview, and nothing is kept on a server.";
    ViewData["BodyClass"] = "legal-page-body";
    ViewData["SolidHeader"] = true;
    ViewData["SkipHref"] = "#privacy";
    ViewData["SkipText"] = "Skip to privacy";
    ViewData["FooterNote"] = "This notice describes what this version of Portico stores. A reservation here is still a preview.";
}

<article class="wrap legal-page" id="privacy">
    <p class="kicker">The list</p>
    <h1>What Portico keeps</h1>
    <p class="legal-intro">This notice covers the site you are using now. A reservation here is a preview. Nothing is charged, and no account is stored on a server.</p>
    <div class="legal-doc">
        <h2>What this version stores</h2>
        <p>The site does not send your name, email, or stay to a server. A stay you save with the heart is kept in this browser only. Dates and guests you choose are written into the page address, so a link you copy carries that search with it.</p>
        <p>Clearing this browser's saved data removes the stays you marked.</p>

        <h2>A reservation preview</h2>
        <p>Confirm reservation asks for a name, an email, an optional phone number, and an optional note for the property. The form stays in the browser long enough to show a reference number. It is not a booking, it is not emailed, and it is not kept after you leave the page.</p>

        <h2>When booking is real</h2>
        <p>A later version will store the guest's name, email, phone if you give one, the note you wrote, the property, the room, the dates, the number of guests, and the stay total. Portico will use that to hold the stay and to send the confirmation. Portico will not sell it.</p>

        <h2>Photographs</h2>
        <p>Photographs on this site are from Unsplash and are used for this design study. They are not offered as pictures of a stay Portico is selling today.</p>

        <p class="legal-updated">Last updated 12 October 2026. The <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Terms">terms</a> say what a price and a reservation mean. Questions about one stay are answered on that stay's page.</p>
    </div>
</article>
